    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two changed-fraction clues can determine x and y.\n\nSuppose (x+1)/(y+1)=2/3 and (x−1)/(y−1)=1/2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Cross-multiply each clue:\n3x+3 = 2y+2 → 3x−2y = −1\n2x−2 = y−1 → 2x−y = 1\n\nSolve the two linear equations to get x=3,y=5. Original fraction=3/5.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
